   "title": "Switching schematic",
   "page": 5,
   "description": "The test set-up for switching times. The LED is pulsed at 10 mA, 10 kHz and 50 % duty cycle. The phototransistor works as a common-emitter switch: RL pulls the collector up to a 5 V supply, the emitter is grounded, the base pin is left open, and VO is taken at the collector.",
