 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Structure",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Inside each package a GaAs infrared LED shines on a silicon NPN phototransistor. The transistor's base is wired out to pin 6, while pin 3 is unused."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Applications",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Suited to detecting AC mains, driving reed relays, feedback in switch-mode supplies, detecting telephone ringing, isolating logic grounds, and coupling logic signals while rejecting high-frequency noise. The part interfaces with the common logic families."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Agency approvals",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "UL file E52744; BSI to EN 60065:2002 and EN 60950:2000; FIMKO to EN 60065, EN 60335 and EN 60950 under certificate 25156. RoHS (2002/95/EC) and WEEE (2002/96/EC) compliant, lead-free."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Saturated and non-saturated CTR",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The saturated CTR (VCE = 0.4 V) and the non-saturated CTR (VCE = 10 V) are both expressed relative to the CTR at VCE = 10 V, IF = 10 mA, 25 °C. The saturated ratio peaks near IF = 10 mA and falls at higher currents; the non-saturated ratio keeps rising up to 60 mA. Both are lower at 50 °C, 70 °C and 85 °C than at 25 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching time definitions",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Output times are taken where VO crosses 1.5 V. tPHL runs from the LED switching on to VO falling through the threshold and is made up of a delay tD and the fall tR; tPLH runs from the LED switching off to VO rising through it, made up of a storage time tS and the rise tF. With a larger collector load tPLH grows from about 7 µs at 0.33 kΩ to about 350 µs at 100 kΩ, while tPHL settles at about 1.5 µs."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Dip soldering at up to 260 °C for no more than 10 s, with the solder at least 1.5 mm from the seating plane."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "The top of the package carries three lines: the part number (4N35 for example), the UL recognition mark, and V YWW 24."
  }
 ],
